From: ahmedsaed <ahmedsaed2652003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux-samsung-a51: enable options needed by Docker

Docker's contrib/check-config.sh reported these "Generally Necessary"
options missing: CGROUP_DEVICE, VETH, BRIDGE, BRIDGE_NETFILTER,
IP6_NF_NAT, IP6_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE, NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE,
NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_IPVS, POSIX_MQUEUE. Also enable CGROUP_PIDS and the
CHECKSUM target. Generated with scripts/config + "make olddefconfig" on
the kernel source, so all dependencies are satisfied; the kernel build's
'yes "" | make oldconfig' would otherwise drop unmet options silently.

Base: pmaports 78e02f370c4e90f53e11fc3d728e3c67fdbaeab6
---
diff --git a/device/archived/linux-samsung-a51/APKBUILD b/device/archived/linux-samsung-a51/APKBUILD
index 388aacd90c..d302a3b87a 100644
--- a/device/archived/linux-samsung-a51/APKBUILD
+++ b/device/archived/linux-samsung-a51/APKBUILD
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 maintainer=""
 pkgname=linux-samsung-a51
 pkgver=4.14.113
-pkgrel=0
+pkgrel=1
 pkgdesc="Samsung Galaxy A51 kernel fork"
 arch="aarch64"
 _carch="arm64"
